<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"QAPage","mainEntity":{"@type":"Question","name":"Handbrake only uses 50% CPU with a Threadripper 9960X","text":"\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eHi,\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eI am using an AMD Ryzen Threadripper 9960X with Windows 10 LTSC IoT.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eWhen I run Handbrake 1.10.2 (2025090600) with the H.265 MKV 2160p60 4K for example, it only runs at 50% cpu.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eI contrast, when running with an Intel Core i9-14900K that is harder to drive with a mix of performance and economy cores, it reaches 100%.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eHow can I optimize the 9960X usage?\u003c/p\u003e","upvoteCount":1,"answerCount":4,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eIsn't a good thing to leave it as the source?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eLeaving it variable leaves it the same as the source always (subject to the framerate cap, if you specify one).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eI did not put them here, at least not now. If they are not standard, it could be a remnant several years old that I forgot about, but I doubt it: I used a standard preset without any change.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eI'd remove it all, although I don't think much of it (other than maybe rect) is making a difference on CPU utilization.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eI'm chasing the best overall speed for a given quality. CPU utilization seemed slow compared to my older platform, but that's not the goal, just an indicator that the CPU might not be used in the optimum way.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eThe primary control for quality is the quality target (RF).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eIMO there's only two x265 presets that make any sense: veryfast or slow. The others are poor tradeoffs.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eThe comparisons to the other platform with heterogenous cores that lack SMT is misguided and misleading.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eIf the utilization really bothers you, you could disable SMT, since the video encoders are well optimized and a bunch of additional threads with no additional execution resources behind them typically doesn't help much.\u003c/p\u003e","upvoteCount":0,"url":"https://github.com/HandBrake/HandBrake/discussions/7311#discussioncomment-14545082"}}}</script>




    

      
    

