    <td
      class="d-block color-fg-default comment-body markdown-body js-comment-body"
      
    >
        <p dir="auto">AV1 is a bit faster at 60% on AMD, and still 100% on Intel. But I prefer to use H.265, AV1 might not work on all devices.</p>
<p dir="auto">I dug a little after your response, and learned about AVX512 and multi-CCD, terms that I did not know, asking Grok and sending the logs before bothering you. I got an interesting answer because you pointed me in the right direction.</p>
<p dir="auto">It turns out that my Handbrake build does not use AVX512, but despite that and hitting a 50% cpu limit,  the 9960X already runs 30% faster than the 14900K.</p>
<p dir="auto">Where can I find a build that supports it? Maybe AMD optimized?</p>
<p dir="auto">That should lead to some nice improvements already, and I'll start tweaking about using threads more efficiently after doing that.</p>
<p dir="auto">I can send the log if you want, but better not to waste your time with it until I get the appropriate build.</p>
    </td>
  </tr>

    </tbody>
  </table>
