    >
        <p dir="auto"><a href="https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22591441/test4K-with.avx512.log.txt">test4K-with avx512 log.txt</a><br>
<a href="https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22591442/test4K-without.avx512.log.txt">test4K-without avx512 log.txt</a></p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto">Ah classic, not even using the preset you mentioned... this is why we want logs.</p>
</blockquote>
<p dir="auto">I made several runs with several presets, I just sent you the last. I did use the preset I mentioned the first time.</p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto">Disable comb detection and deinterlace since your 24 fps content isn't,</p>
</blockquote>
<p dir="auto">I always do for real work, here it was just a quick test.</p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto">and I wouldn't bother with forcing fixed framerate.</p>
</blockquote>
<p dir="auto">Isn't a good thing to leave it as the source?</p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto">Preset matters less when you've got a bunch of dubious copypasta in the advanced options overriding it.</p>
</blockquote>
<p dir="auto">I did not put them here, at least not now. If they are not standard, it could be a remnant several years old that I forgot about, but I doubt it: I used a standard preset without any change.</p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto">Put asm=avx512 in the advanced video encoder options box to enable it, although it's disabled by default for a reason, it generally doesn't help especially below 4K and can hurt.</p>
</blockquote>
<p dir="auto">I made a small run. As you can see from the logs, it gave a 5.5% speed boost. Not earth shattering, but worth using it.</p>
<p dir="auto">CPU is still around 54%.</p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto">If you're just chasing CPU utilization, try faster presets too.</p>
</blockquote>
<p dir="auto">I'm chasing the best overall speed for a given quality. CPU utilization seemed slow compared to my older platform, but that's not the goal, just an indicator that the CPU <em>might</em> not be used in the optimum way.</p>
<p dir="auto">If this is the optimum for this platform, that's fine. It allows for less heat than running at 100%.</p>
<p dir="auto">But if there is room for speed improvement like above, I'll take it.</p>
<p dir="auto">What do you think? Using the avx512 option was a good suggestion, maybe there is something else?</p>
    </td>
  </tr>

    </tbody>
  </table>
